{
  "title": "Medusa \u2014 e-commerce (33,822\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Medusa\nDomain: e-commerce | Scale: large | Stars: 33,822\nProblem: Medusa is a flexible, open-source commerce platform that provides building blocks and a customizable framework for building advanced digital commerce applications without reinventing core commerce logic.\nTarget users: E-commerce developers, Commerce platform builders, B2B and DTC store operators, Marketplace creators, PoS system developers, Service business platforms\nCore features: Modular commerce framework with customizable core logic; Open-source commerce modules available on npm; Multi-tenant and advanced B2B capabilities; Managed cloud deployment and scaling (Medusa Cloud); Extensible integration ecosystem; Admin UI and design system\nIntegrations: Payment providers, Shipping integrations, Third-party commerce APIs, Custom provider system\nTech stack: React with Storybook, TypeScript + Node.js with Express, TypeScript + Not specified in manifest (likely PostgreSQL based on typical Medusa deployments) + Medusa Cloud (managed), Docker-ready\nKey libraries: Express, TypeScript, React, Jest, SWC, Rollup, Storybook, Testing Library\nArchitecture: microservices\nDesign lessons:\n- Monorepo workspace structure with modular packages enables pluggable commerce modules and provider system for maximum extensibility\n- Separation of core framework, modules, admin UI, and CLI into distinct packages allows independent versioning and selective adoption\n- Comprehensive test and build tooling (Jest, SWC, Rollup) across workspace ensures quality and performance at scale\n- Design system and component library (Storybook) shared across admin and integrations promotes consistency in commerce UX",
